    "content": "The UConn Huskies men’s basketball team has won six NCAA National Championships, with titles in 1999, 2004, 2011, 2014, 2023, and 2024. They are a powerhouse program, having won all six titles since 1999, including back-to-back championships in 2023 and 2024 under coach Dan Hurley. UConn Men’s Championship Game Results: 1999: Defeated Duke, 77–74 2004: Defeated Georgia Tech, 82–73 2011: Defeated Butler, 53–41 2014: Defeated Kentucky, 60–54 2023: Defeated San Diego State, 76–59 2024: Defeated Purdue, 75–60 These six championships tie UConn for the third-most all-time, behind only UCLA and Kentucky.",
